{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1092747-permanent-paradox","id":1092747,"title":"permanent paradox","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-15T05:13:54-07:00","id":1092747,"title":"permanent paradox","content":"If I were to use prime 3 and life 3 to infuse my patterns with prime in order to soak and and deal agg damage, however I'm not making it last permanently but for a certain duration. It wouldn't give me a permanent point of paradox, correct?<br /> Permadox usually comes from permanent, vulgar buffs and the likes right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T05:45:32-07:00","id":1092757,"title":"","content":"Permanent Paradox, at least in M20, only comes from permanent changes - Enhancements, Cybernetic implants, Life effects that the player made permanent with XP expeditures and such things.<br /> <br /> Temporary changes, depending on their nature, are affected by Pattern Bleeding - requiring you to spend one Quintessence per day (after the first), or suffer one dot of unsoakable damage that cannot be magically healed.<br /> <br /> The only way to avoid Pattern Bleeding is to use Life 5, which allows perfect transformation of the life pattern - but unless the effect is made permanent with XP (again giving permanent paradox), it is a running effect that can be detected and unwoven/counterspelled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-15-2017, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T05:54:44-07:00","id":1092761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1092747-permanent-paradox?p=1092757#post1092757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Permanent Paradox, at least in M20, only comes from permanent changes - Enhancements, Cybernetic implants, Life effects that the player made permanent with XP expeditures and such things.<br /> <br /> Temporary changes, depending on their nature, are affected by Pattern Bleeding - requiring you to spend one Quintessence per day (after the first), or suffer one dot of unsoakable damage that cannot be magically healed.<br /> <br /> The only way to avoid Pattern Bleeding is to use Life 5, which allows perfect transformation of the life pattern - but unless the effect is made permanent with XP (again giving permanent paradox), it is a running effect that can be detected and unwoven/counterspelled.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK pattern bleeding is caused by altering attributes per say, such as boosting your attributes with life 3 without paying XP.<br /> However in the case of infusing my patterns with prime and not mutating the patterns in anyway but simply reinforcing them, I suppose that it's safe to assume that there'd be no pattern bleeding and no permadox since it's not permanent, correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T06:05:47-07:00","id":1092767,"title":"","content":"Yes, if the life pattern itself does not get changed, there is no pattern bleeding. So, yes to both your statements <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T11:22:49-07:00","id":1092881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1092747-permanent-paradox#post1092747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to use prime 3 and life 3 to infuse my patterns with prime in order to soak and and deal agg damage, however I'm not making it last permanently but for a certain duration. It wouldn't give me a permanent point of paradox, correct?<br /> Permadox usually comes from permanent, vulgar buffs and the likes right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to point out, that the \u201cpermanent\u201c in Permadox refers to the paradox points and not to the source of the points being a permanent effect.<br /> If you buff you stamina to 6 you get 1 Permadox as long as the effect is active.<br /> Pattern bleeding is a thing whenever your pattern is altered for a time greater than 1 day.<br /> IMHO it matters not in the slightest if you reinforce the quintessential flow, mutate it, or simply alter it. If you use magick to do something with your pattern for a week, then you bleed 6 times.<br /> <br /> Your effect is tricky. Causing agg is not a problem, but soaking agg can be vulgar.<br /> If you want to make sure the effect remains coincidental, then it could be done if the soak agg part is only in effect if soaking this particular case of agg damage is coincidental.<br /> The other way round: if you want to make sure that you can soak agg anytime, go for a vulgar effect.<br /> In the latter case I think that a point of Permadox is in order.<br /> Pattern bleeding occurs regardless of vulgarity.<br /> <br /> If it wasn't that way, nobody would go for permanent alterations. They would opt for long duration effects. Enhancement (background) would be pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T22:50:47-07:00","id":1093114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1092747-permanent-paradox?p=1092881#post1092881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you buff you stamina to 6 you get 1 Permadox as long as the effect is active.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes. I forgot the case of stats going over 5! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T10:31:44-07:00","id":1101674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1092747-permanent-paradox?p=1092881#post1092881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just wanted to point out, that the \u201cpermanent\u201c in Permadox refers to the paradox points and not to the source of the points being a permanent effect.<br /> If you buff you stamina to 6 you get 1 Permadox as long as the effect is active.<br /> Pattern bleeding is a thing whenever your pattern is altered for a time greater than 1 day.<br /> IMHO it matters not in the slightest if you reinforce the quintessential flow, mutate it, or simply alter it. If you use magick to do something with your pattern for a week, then you bleed 6 times.<br /> <br /> Your effect is tricky. Causing agg is not a problem, but soaking agg can be vulgar.<br /> If you want to make sure the effect remains coincidental, then it could be done if the soak agg part is only in effect if soaking this particular case of agg damage is coincidental.<br /> The other way round: if you want to make sure that you can soak agg anytime, go for a vulgar effect.<br /> In the latter case I think that a point of Permadox is in order.<br /> Pattern bleeding occurs regardless of vulgarity.<br /> <br /> If it wasn't that way, nobody would go for permanent alterations. They would opt for long duration effects. Enhancement (background) would be pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hear me out, however. The book specifies that pattern bleeding is caused when u mutate/alter your pattern.<br /> Now, if you would read the prime 3 abilities in m20 core book, it clearly says &quot;empowers your pattern to deal and soak aggravated damage.&quot; - I by no means alter my pattern by doing so. I reinforce it, I empower it. It doesn't undergo any sort of mutations or changes. I do not bestow upon myself a new ability of some sort.<br /> Soaking damage is smth anyone can do, it's within everyone's pattern. I merely strengthen that ability.<br /> <br /> You see where I'm going? I simply energize my pattern with prime in order to soak agg and deal agg.<br /> Hence, IMO it wouldn't cause pattern bleeding. However, A permanent paradox point surely is in order, with that I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","user":"MowtekPvP","date":". 06-08-2017, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T10:59:29-07:00","id":1101683,"title":"","content":"Your pattern has been changed from &quot;not empowered&quot; to &quot;empowered&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> And in a way that is likely Vulgar: As has been said, resisting Agg it's always vulgar, but I would say that dealing Aggravate it's vulgar too in this case. Why?, because the body normaly causes Contundent damage. Contundent it's very different from Vulgar, humans can't soak Aggravated, and it heals like Lethal, thus your punches not only have the potential of causing much more damage and kill faster, but also heal slower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T11:45:49-07:00","id":1101696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1092747-permanent-paradox?p=1101674#post1101674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hear me out, however. The book specifies that pattern bleeding is caused when u mutate/alter your pattern.<br /> Now, if you would read the prime 3 abilities in m20 core book, it clearly says &amp;quot;empowers your pattern to deal and soak aggravated damage.&amp;quot; - I by no means alter my pattern by doing so. I reinforce it, I empower it. It doesn't undergo any sort of mutations or changes. I do not bestow upon myself a new ability of some sort.<br /> Soaking damage is smth anyone can do, it's within everyone's pattern. I merely strengthen that ability.<br /> <br /> You see where I'm going? I simply energize my pattern with prime in order to soak agg and deal agg.<br /> Hence, IMO it wouldn't cause pattern bleeding. However, A permanent paradox point surely is in order, with that I agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>My body can heal itself, I simply strenghten that ability so I can heal in an instant.<br /> <br /> My body has the ability to withstand aging(temperature/lack of x), I empower my pattern to greatly increase this natural ability.<br /> <br /> IMHO it is all the same: you change your pattern. You make an alteration. If you wouldn't alter anything, then you wouldn't have an effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}